# Optional: real GitHub sign-in in local cloud dev. Without this file, dev
# login (DEV_AUTH) covers everything except the real OAuth redirect dance.
#
# EASY MODE — run once, everything below happens automatically:
#   bun run setup:github-oauth
#
# Manual mode: create a GitHub App (or classic OAuth app) at
# https://github.com/settings/apps with callback URL
# http://localhost:8787/api/auth/callback/github (GitHub Apps also need
# Account Permissions → Email addresses → Read-only), then copy this file to
# .dev.vars (gitignored) in your MAIN clone — every worktree's `bun run dev`
# reads the main clone's copy automatically (a worktree-local .dev.vars takes
# precedence if you need one to differ).
# `bun run dev` normally assigns each worktree its own deterministic cloud
# port. To test this real OAuth callback in one worktree, launch that worktree
# with CODEVISOR_DEV_CLOUD_PORT=8787. Other worktrees continue to use their own
# ports and the built-in development account.
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret
